<header><p class="enc-kicker">People / group</p><h1 class="enc-title">Swahili</h1><p class="enc-meta">Also known as Swahili merchants</p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">The Swahili are a people of the East African coast, whose culture developed through interaction between <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/bantu-peoples">Bantu-speaking</a> Africans and Arab and Persian traders. Swahili merchants traded gold, <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/ivory-trade">ivory</a> and other goods. The <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/mutapa-empire">Mutapa Empire</a> and <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/rozvi-empire">Rozvi Empire</a> profiles describe their role in trade with the interior.</p></div>
